Me too, although I can not promise how much time I will have to work on 
such projects, but it will surely be some constant amount, even if it 
may be very little.

Continuing on the "language to rewrite" war, I'd prefer C++, because 
this not only makes data structures easier with STL, but it also makes 
code cleaner as compared to C (at least it seems to me it's easier to do 
cleaner and better structured code).  I wouldn't want Java, because to 
me it is just a "poor C++" (at least if you make sensible use of C++ 
such that the "protection" Java offers against certain poor coding 
techniques does not  matter) and I'd only consider it for rare cases 
like when I want an Applet for a Webpage or a program that needs to run 
on multiple platforms *without recompiling*.

But C would also be fine, if we adopt a good style; it seems there are 
really some people out there who are in favor of C.  Another idea (just 
because I recently worked with it) could be to do some mixed languages 
programming, like basic engine code in C/C++ and some of the 
NetHack-content atop of it using a scripting language like Guile for 
controlling the engine with the actual gameplay?

